From c259e8840f8f7a77f56525d98d05de194c4d4c28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:13:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MiniMax-M3.1-Flash: qk-norm/RoPE paged writer, fp32 router
 GEMV and block-table mirror (T8 kernels)

Adds minimax_m3_rows.cu: tf_mm3_rows (per-head Gemma RMSNorm of q, k and the index
heads, partial RoPE with float64 angles, q and the index query to scratch, k, v and
the index key straight into paged K/V/IK by block table; decode positions or pos0;
rope layout, index rope, fp16/bf16 index input, weight offset and norm rounding are
launch parameters) and tf_mm3_router_bf16/f32 (fp32 router logits, fixed per-output
reduction order independent of row count, tiling and neighbours).

Zig: cuda/minimax_m3_rows.zig wrapper and the Mirror of the block tables (device copy
with pool.Upload-compatible call, per-row row_tab offsets for shared windows, single
stream table pointers), std-only minimax_m3_rows_geom.zig arithmetic, families/
minimax_m3/rows.zig (Switches -> launch parameters), launch records from nvcc 13.0.88
for sm_80/86/89/120/121, contract test types with float64 references (compile-checked),
host twins with planted mutants, and `zig build test-minimax-rows`. No GPU has run any
kernel; nothing here claims GPU correctness. Written from the plan's formulas.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QguKy82jHfqdgzDsrrC5xs
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
